# ── AI Provider (required for Phase 3 matching: embeddings + resonance synthesis) ──
# Gemini is the default and runs on Google's free tier. Get a key at
# https://aistudio.google.com/apikey — no credit card, no billing account.
# gemini-embedding-001 emits 1536-dimension vectors, matching profiles.profile_embedding.
GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key_here

# Model overrides — Google retires and renames Flash models fairly often, so these
# are configurable without a code change. Omit to use the defaults shown.
# GEMINI_EMBEDDING_MODEL=gemini-embedding-001
# GEMINI_CHAT_MODEL=gemini-3.5-flash-lite

# Optional paid alternative. Used ONLY when no Gemini key is set.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...

# Omit all of them to run in local demo mode. Leaving placeholder text in place is
# treated the same as omitting the value entirely (see lib/config.ts).

# Supabase Configuration (Phase 2 & beyond)
# Project URL: Dashboard → Connect, or Settings → Data API
# Client key:  Settings → API Keys → Publishable key (sb_publishable_...)
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_...
# Legacy fallback (optional): NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJ...
# Secret key — SERVER ONLY, never expose to the browser. Bypasses Row Level Security.
# Required for matching, consent transitions and messaging: these read candidate
# profiles and write match/conversation rows that no client policy grants.
# Settings → API Keys → Secret keys.
SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=sb_secret_...

# Legacy fallback (optional): the JWT-based service_role key. Supabase is retiring
# anon/service_role keys by the end of 2026 — prefer SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY above.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=eyJ...

# Moderation queue access, comma-separated. Anyone signed in with one of these
# addresses can open /admin/reports; everyone else gets a 404.
#
# NOT a flag on the profiles table: the "Users manage own profile" policy gates
# which row you may write, not which columns, so a user can PATCH any field on
# their own profile — an is_admin column there would be self-grantable.
# Leave unset and the queue is closed to everyone.
# ADMIN_EMAILS=you@example.com,cofounder@example.com

# Public origin, used for canonical URLs, Open Graph image URLs, robots and sitemap.
# Must be the real domain in production — a wrong value makes every shared link
# preview fetch the wrong host and render as a bare URL.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://mindmate.site

# Set on any deployment that is live but should not be found yet: robots.txt
# becomes a blanket Disallow and every page carries noindex/nofollow.
#
# Server-only, and read at module scope in app/robots.ts and app/layout.tsx, so
# it is baked in at build time — clearing it needs a redeploy, not just an
# env-var save. Link previews still work; scrapers read Open Graph tags directly
# and never consult robots.txt.
# SITE_NOINDEX=1

# Cloudflare Turnstile site key (public by design — the secret goes in Supabase,
# not here). Supabase → Settings → Authentication → Bot and Abuse Protection is
# what actually verifies the token; this only renders the widget.
#
# Signup never passes through this app — auth-form.tsx calls supabase.auth.signUp()
# on the browser client, so the request goes straight to <project>.supabase.co.
# No middleware, WAF rule or proxy in front of the site can see it, which is why
# the CAPTCHA has to live inside Supabase.
#
# Add `localhost` to the widget's hostname list in Cloudflare, or enabling the
# Supabase toggle breaks local signup. Unset here, the widget renders nothing.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=0x4AAAAAAA...
